#lang r7rs
;; docs/archive/r7rs-dynamic-environment-shared-across-threads.md: the R7RS
;; dynamic environment on five threads at once.  The handler stack, the wind
;; stack and the parameter cells were process globals, so a raise on one
;; thread called a handler another thread had installed ("continuation
;; invoked after its call/cc prompt returned"), a pop on one removed
;; another's ("uncaught exception: boom"), an escape ran another thread's
;; dynamic-wind `after`, and a parameterize on one thread changed the value
;; every other thread read.  Every run failed.  They are per thread now.
(import (scheme base) (scheme write) (dynsteps) (turmeric dyncrew))
(crew-start)
(define mine (spin 20000))
(crew-join)
(write (list mine (crew-total))) (newline)
